  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Calculate the product $D{I}_{2}$ given that ${I}_{2}$ is the $2\\times 2$ identity matrix and\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\n| $D\\cdot {I}_{2}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Any matrix, when multiplied by an identity matrix, remains unchanged (assuming that the multiplication is well defined).\n\nThe matrix $D$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and ${I}_{2}$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix too. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication is well defined and \n\n$$\nD\\cdot {I}_{2}=D=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
